# Requests to try the API by hand (Visual Studio, Rider, or VS Code with the REST Client extension).
# Run the API first: dotnet run --project src/EmployerRequests.Api

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5080

### The first page, newest first
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/requests?page=1&pageSize=20

### Combined filters, sorted by priority
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/requests?status=New&status=Waiting&priority=High&sortBy=priority&sortDirection=desc&pageSize=10

### Summary of everything – served from the cache after the first call
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/requests/summary

### Summary of the high-priority requests – calculated on every call
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/requests/summary?priority=High

### One request – copy its rowVersion for the status change below
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/requests/1

### Its history
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/requests/1/history

### Change the status. Send it twice with the same rowVersion: the second answer is 409.
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/requests/1/status
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-Name: dana

{
  "status": "InProgress",
  "rowVersion": "PASTE-THE-ROWVERSION-HERE"
}

### Bulk change – every request gets its own outcome
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/requests/status
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-Name: dana

{
  "status": "Waiting",
  "items": [
    { "id": 2, "rowVersion": "PASTE-THE-ROWVERSION-HERE" },
    { "id": 3, "rowVersion": "PASTE-THE-ROWVERSION-HERE" }
  ]
}

### Invalid parameters – 400 with the field names
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/requests?pageSize=500&sortBy=password
